+## Spec of record left stale
+
+The design doc (linked from INDEX.md and named as "Design:" in the onboarding spec's new Post-Implementation note) asks in its own `## Post-Implementation Notes` section for a dated note on anything that diverged; that section is empty at head. The bead hg-lnw.21 exempts historical records from its remedy-string sweep, so the stale remedy alone is acceptable, but the design text now contradicts the shipped behaviour on several normative points, most of them the design-roast r2 confirmed items that run.md records as "designRoast r2 fixed" while the fixes landed only in beads and code:
+
+- §4.2 says a rebind `NotFound` is an "already-placed" done answer; the code records `NotFound` as a definitive refusal under `rebind_refused:<clone>` (effects.rs rebind executor; verification-matrix lists `NotFound` as definitive), and `SeatAlreadyResolved` is the done answer.
+- §3 gives the resurrect op key as `resurrect:<clone>:<epoch>:<replace seat id or none>`; the code adds `:<refusal count>`.
+- §3 lists no `SeatAlreadyResolved` outcome; the adapter maps it to done.
+- §3 ties the invitation reset to the resurrect success transition only; hg-lnw.15 applies it on every keyless resurrect acknowledgement, and CURRENT-DESIGN says rejected rows are not re-issued, which §3's no-op claim does not cover.
+- §4 table rows for adopted keyless seats say the relaunch "waits until the seat is placed or the grace expires" for the session-captured (resume) case; the shipped rule, documented in README and CURRENT-DESIGN, is that a resumed relaunch waits the full 90 s grace.
+- §3 and §4.5 print the remedy without the `human` namespace, which threads 3.6.0 refuses (hg-lnw.21).
+- The hg-lnw.23 change (retry `agent.start` under a pane-qualified name on `agent_name_taken`) is not recorded.
